      "content": "that's a fair point, but it feels like you're still trying to balance them perfectly. if a policy causes massive growth but leaves a huge chunk of the population behind, wouldn't most modern economists agree that the policy was fundamentally a failure? like, isn't the inequality side seen as the more definitive outcome of that era?",
